Let's go step by step.

Step 1: Attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha.

Action: attach_task_profile
Parameters: ?candidate - candidate_entity ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile
Precondition: (candidate_created ?candidate) (vehicle_allocated ?candidate) (route_task_profile_available ?route_task_profile)
We have candidate_created origin_availability_alpha true.
vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha true.
route_task_profile_alpha available? Assume true (not in init but we assume). We'll treat as available.

Thus we can do: (attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Effect: candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha, and not route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha.

Now route_task_profile_alpha becomes unavailable (linked). Good.

Step 2: Confirm candidate preparedness for origin_availability_alpha.

Action: confirm_candidate_preparedness
Parameters: ?candidate - candidate_entity ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile
Precondition: (candidate_created ?candidate) (vehicle_allocated ?candidate) (candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile) (not (candidate_prepared ?candidate))
We have candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, candidate_task_profile_linked (just added), not candidate_prepared (initially false). So we can do: (confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Effect: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha.

Now origin_availability_alpha prepared.

Step 3: Activate origin node.

Action: activate_origin_node
Parameters: ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile
Precondition: (candidate_prepared ?origin_availability) (candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile) (origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node) (not (origin_node_ready ?origin_node)) (not (origin_node_occupied ?origin_node))
We have candidate_prepared true, candidate_task_profile_linked true, origin_availability_node_linked true, origin_node_ready? Not in init, so false (so not origin_node_ready true). origin_node_occupied? Not in init, false. So preconditions satisfied.

Effect: origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha.

Thus (activate_origin_node origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Now origin_node_ready true.

Step 4: Load origin payload.

Action: load_origin_payload
Parameters: ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?payload_unit - cargo_payload
Precondition: (candidate_prepared ?origin_availability) (origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node) (cargo_available ?payload_unit) (not (origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability))
We have candidate_prepared true, origin_availability_node_linked true, cargo_available true, origin_availability_locked? Not yet, so false. So we can load.

Effect: (origin_node_occupied ?origin_node) (origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability) (cargo_available ?payload_unit) (not (origin_payload_linked ?origin_availability ?payload_unit))

Thus after load: origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available remains true (since effect adds cargo_available), origin_payload_linked becomes false (since not). Note: we had no origin_payload_linked before, so not is fine.

Thus (load_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)

Step 5: Assign operator to origin.

Action: assign_operator_resource
Parameters: ?candidate - candidate_entity ?operator_resource - operator_resource
Precondition: (candidate_prepared ?candidate) (operator_available ?operator_resource)
We have candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha true, operator_available driver_operator_alpha true.

Effect: (candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource) (not (operator_available ?operator_resource))

Thus (assign_operator_resource origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha)

Now origin_availability_alpha linked to operator, operator not available.

Step 6: Lock origin availability.

Action: lock_origin_availability
Parameters: ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?operator_resource - operator_resource
Precondition: (candidate_prepared ?origin_availability) (candidate_operator_linked ?origin_availability ?operator_resource) (origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node) (origin_node_ready ?origin_node) (not (origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability))
We have candidate_prepared true, candidate_operator_linked true (just assigned), origin_availability_node_linked true, origin_node_ready true (from activate), origin_availability_locked? Not yet, false. So we can lock.

Effect: (origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability) (origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability)

Thus (lock_origin_availability origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha driver_operator_alpha)

Now origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true (already true from load, but effect sets again).

Step 7: Release operator from origin (to make free for destination).

Action: release_operator_resource
Parameters: ?candidate - candidate_entity ?operator_resource - operator_resource
Precondition: (candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource)
We have that.

Effect: (operator_available ?operator_resource) (not (candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource))

Thus (release_operator_resource origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha)

Now operator available again.

Step 8: Activate destination node.

Action: activate_destination_node
Parameters: ?destination_availability - destination_candidate_availability ?destination_node - destination_node ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile
Precondition: (candidate_prepared ?destination_availability) (candidate_task_profile_linked ?destination_availability ?route_task_profile) (destination_availability_node_linked ?destination_availability ?destination_node) (not (destination_node_ready ?destination_node)) (not (destination_node_occupied ?destination_node))
