Now destination node occupied, destination_availability_confirmed true.

Step 10: Assign operator to destination.

Action: assign_operator_resource destination_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha

Precondition: candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha true, operator_available driver_operator_alpha true (we released earlier). So okay.

Effect: candidate_operator_linked destination_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha, operator not available.

Step 11: Lock destination availability.

Action: lock_destination_availability
Parameters: ?destination_availability - destination_candidate_availability ?destination_node - destination_node ?operator_resource - operator_resource
Precondition: (candidate_prepared ?destination_availability) (candidate_operator_linked ?destination_availability ?operator_resource) (destination_availability_node_linked ?destination_availability ?destination_node) (destination_node_ready ?destination_node) (not (destination_availability_locked ?destination_availability))
We have candidate_prepared true, candidate_operator_linked true (just assigned), destination_availability_node_linked true, destination_node_ready true (from activation), destination_availability_locked? false. So we can lock.

Effect: (destination_availability_locked ?destination_availability) (destination_availability_confirmed ?destination_availability)

Thus (lock_destination_availability destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha driver_operator_alpha)

Now destination locked and confirmed.

Step 12: Release operator from destination (optional but maybe not needed further). We'll release to keep operator free, though not required.

Action: release_operator_resource destination_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha

Now operator available.

Step 13: Assemble transport leg.

